<title>HUNGARY: MOL hits record as investors see it cheap.</title>
<headline>MOL hits record as investors see it cheap.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hungarian oil and gas company MOL Rt rose to record territory on Wednesday as it was considered one of the still undervalued papers of the Budapest Stock Exchange, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;MOL, along with (pharmaceuticals) Richter and OTP Bank is rising mainly because the market still thinks it is relatively cheap,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The trader said he was not aware of any fresh news about MOL which has been one of the strongest gainers of the past few days.</p>
<p>MOL opened at 3,600 forints and peaked at 3,790 forints but by 1122 GMT it retreated to 3,660.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
